{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2909","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2909","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2909\",\"parent_revision\":\"50c3014c5f2014592ff7cad05afe631d19e34894e48d8154ca2635cb17c9414d\",\"root_revision\":\"50c3014c5f2014592ff7cad05afe631d19e34894e48d8154ca2635cb17c9414d\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTwo findings from independent review of PR #2902 (fix(development-harness): heal stale empty BacklogItem.reference on load). Not blocking that PR \u2014 it's correct and tested \u2014 but worth a proper follow-up:\\n\\n1. Reuse: _stable_reference() in github_work_items.py duplicates near-identical 'derive fallback reference' logic already present at memory_backend.py:150 and sqlite_backend.py:222 (item.reference = item.reference or item.issue or uuid.uuid4().hex). Three independent implementations, with different fallback strategies (deterministic sha256(title) in the GitHub backend vs random uuid4 in the other two) and no shared helper. A future change to the priority order needs manual application in three places.\\n\\n2. Architecture (altitude review): BacklogItem.reference is a plain field, NOT synced by the _sync_metadata validator (unlike priority/issue and the other flat-accessor fields) and BacklogItemMetadata has no reference field to sync with. PR #2902 heals this at the GitHub backend's specific read boundary (load_records() in github_work_items.py). sqlite_backend.py's list_work_items()/get_work_item() reads raw persisted JSON via model_validate_json with zero healing \u2014 structurally the same latent bug, currently only safe because put_work_item() is the sole write funnel (verified via grep, no other write site exists) \u2014 an incidental protection, not a structural one. beads_backend.py already does the right thing: it force-derives reference fresh from issue.id on every list call, never trusting a persisted value.\\n\\nRecommendation: fold the reference-derivation invariant into BacklogItem itself (e.g. a validator/method on the model, mirroring how beads_backend already derives fresh rather than trusts-cached), so it self-heals at construction time across every backend and every future write path, rather than being healed per-read-call-site in one specific backend module.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Not specified\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-16\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **refactor(backlog-mcp): consolidate triplicated reference-fallback logic and move reference healing to backlogitem model layer** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"7ed3c70feeda8bf7d080b179a738ea8db8167c6b35aa57b037f090e5c32e8744\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS6wYA\"}"}